{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jt5pfkfiv6kb4igdittvcoc4tp3w3oneowiio4v5lcgkea7gtmzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\nA single translation unit (34 lines) exporting exactly one symbol: `synth_pair` — the minimp3 polyphase synthesis pair, plus a `static` helper `mp3d_scale_pcm`.\n\n## Phase A — surface mapped\n\n| Artifact | Content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` on both `.so`s: C exports exactly `synth_pair`; Rust exports it too. **Symbol diff empty.** No module was missing, so nothing needed back-filling; `mp3d_scale_pcm` is correctly *not* exported (it's `static`). |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 22 rows. This API has **no error channel** (void return, no asserts, no null/length checks, no enums), so the rejection surface is the two saturation branches, the NaN fall-through, the `s -= (s<0)` correction, and the UB reachable through unvalidated params. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 26 rows over 8 axes derived from the source (`nch` shapes, both accumulation chains, tap index set, accumulator regime, value class, accumulation-order sensitivity, pointer alignment, statelessness). |\n\n**Feature combinations: exactly one.** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` section; `verify_all.sh` derives the powerset mechanically and confirms `n = 0 → 1 combo`.\n\n## Phases B–D — all green\n\nAll tests load **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and call the exported symbols — the Rust is never called directly.\n\n- **26/26 CONFIGS rows** pass, plus a **3,000,000-iteration** soak fuzz.\n- **22/22 ERRORS rows** pass with concrete sentinel assertions (`32767` / `-32768` / `0` / exact wrapped offsets), not \"both failed somehow\". Null-pointer and `int`-overflow UB use subprocess crash-parity, confirmed to genuinely fault (`signal=11` both sides), not silently survive.\n- **Symbol parity** re-derived at test time; `mp3d_scale_pcm` asserted absent from both.\n- Whole suite re-run under **every** configuration (1 feature combo × release *and* debug cdylib).\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n**A real divergence was found and fixed.** With a null `pcm`, the C stores to address 0 → `SIGSEGV`. rustc's debug assertions inject a language-UB check that turns the identical access into a `\"null pointer dereference\"` panic → `SIGABRT`. Invisible in release, so I added `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false` to `Cargo.toml` — the C performs no validation, so the translation must not inject checks the C lacks. Both now terminate with `signal=11` in both profiles.\n\n**A latent doc/test blind spot in my own Phase A.** I initially assumed chain 1 read all 15 stride-64 taps; the C actually reads only the **even** multiples, so the true read set is **23** of 899 slots, not 30. I caught this by transcribing the C into an independent model and diffing it against the real `.so` (`harness_model_matches_c_library`, 4000 vectors). This mattered: every `z` buffer poisons the 876 unread slots with `NaN`, so any tap-index mistake in the translation collapses the Rust accumulator to `0` and diverges loudly — poisoning the wrong slots would have silently weakened every Phase B row.\n\nThe translation itself needed **no changes** to `src/lib.rs`: the accumulation order, `int`-wrapping index arithmetic, saturating-cast-vs-`cvttss2si` NaN behavior, and inclusive clamp boundaries were all already exact."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":754,"cache_read_input_tokens":140691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":754,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b25ad25-11b5-4a0a-b3fb-41a0ffd1f772","uuid":"489f4de7-4d22-453f-a7f2-c155e4dfede1","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:52:09.766Z"}
